---
description: Proposing a new Godlint rule, or reconsidering one previously marked "do not build"
alwaysApply: false
---

Read `docs/skills/propose-a-rule.md` in full and follow it before filing the issue.

Apply the three filters in order: decidable without types; has a specific false-positive case
that configuration can exempt; has a measurable threshold (see `docs/skills/proposing-a-threshold.md`).
File using the `rule_proposal.yml` template's shape — policy problem, blocked, examples, scope,
remediation, false positive, source, definition of done — and verify every cited URL actually
resolves before it goes in the issue. Label with `rule-proposal`, a priority, and any blocker
(`needs-a-fact` / `needs-a-subsystem` / `needs-a-language`).
